{"t": 68.999, "n": 63, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Phase 4 is built: `improve outbox list` and `improve outbox clear` exist, and I marked rows 4.1 to 4.3 done in the plan.\n\nI wrote `test_outbox_verbs.py` first and saw it fail with exit 2 (the verb didn't exist). Then I added `Outbox.entries()` and `Outbox.remove()` in `improve/filing.py`, and the `outbox` sub-verb with its `_outbox` handler in `cli/improve.py`. `test_outbox_verbs.py` and `test_contract_tables.py` pass together (13 tests).\n\nOne choice the spec doesn't state: `list` puts entries with no queue time last, after the oldest-first ones.\n\nI searched the specs for the commands this change exposes. I found no behaviour it makes false.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran tests/test_outbox_verbs.py (failed first, exit 2 as the verb was missing) and tests/test_contract_tables.py; both pass after rows 4.1-4.3 (13 tests). Deviations: none. One choice the spec leaves open: `list` puts entries with no queue time last after the oldest-first ones. Checked specs for the changed commands/fields; no behaviour made false.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "003a2b94-dd07-415f-867e-3c41a5134311"}
